---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Ornament from '../../components/Ornament.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import RelatedPages from '../../components/RelatedPages.astro';
import GetTheApp from '../../components/GetTheApp.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';

const title = 'CardHabit vs Habitica: A Sustainable Alternative to RPG Habit Tracking';
const description = 'How CardHabit compares to Habitica for second-time-around habit builders. Habitica is an open RPG over a custom to-do list. CardHabit is a structured daily card draw built for people who burned out on extreme systems and want sustainable accountability with friends.';

// Content last substantively changed: November 2026. Update by hand when the page changes.
const updated = 'November 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <Breadcrumbs section="Comparisons" name="CardHabit vs Habitica" />
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section style="padding:5rem 1.5rem 3rem;text-align:center;">
      <div style="max-width:780px;margin:0 auto;">
        <p style="font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:10px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.28em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6E1E22;margin:0 0 1.25rem;">
          Comparison
        </p>
        <h1 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(2.4rem,7vw,3.75rem);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-0.015em;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 1.75rem;">
          CardHabit <em style="color:#6E1E22;font-style:italic;">vs Habitica.</em>
        </h1>
        <p style="font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-weight:300;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.7;color:#574B40;max-width:620px;margin:0 auto;">
          Both are gamified habit apps. They're built for different people. Habitica is an open RPG you customize forever. CardHabit is a daily card draw for your life, built for the second-time-around habit builder: someone who read Atomic Habits, tried 75 Hard, and wants a sustainable system with friends involved instead of a fantasy MMO.
        </p>
        <p style="font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:10px;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#645749;margin:1.5rem 0 0;">
          Updated {updated}
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Ornament />

    <section style="padding:3rem 1.5rem;">
      <div style="max-width:780px;margin:0 auto;font-family:'Jost',system-ui,sans-serif;font-weight:300;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;color:#574B40;">
        <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:2rem;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 1.5rem;">The short version</h2>
        <p style="margin:0 0 2rem;">Choose Habitica if you want a deep RPG with parties, boss battles, and a customizable to-do list at its center. Choose CardHabit if you want a tighter daily practice: five cards dealt each morning, commitments you choose, and a binder that fills with every card you finish.</p>

        <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:2rem;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 1.5rem;">At a glance</h2>

        <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:0 0 2rem;">
          <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.95rem;">
            <thead>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.35);">
                <th style="text-align:left;padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#6E1E22;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:0.8rem;">Feature</th>
                <th style="text-align:left;padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#6E1E22;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:0.8rem;">CardHabit</th>
                <th style="text-align:left;padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#6E1E22;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:0.8rem;">Habitica</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Platform</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">iOS</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">iOS, Android, web</td></tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Core mechanic</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Daily 5-card draw</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Custom to-do list</td></tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Social mechanic</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Deal a friend in: share a card, finish it together (2.0)</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Parties, boss battles, group chat</td></tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Classification</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">No classes; your binder shows what you actually did</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">4 chosen classes (Warrior, Mage, Rogue, Healer)</td></tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Categories</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Five suits plus the Joker in 2.0 (Physical, Mind, Nutrition, Recovery, Connection)</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">User-defined</td></tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom:0.5px solid rgba(156, 122, 46, 0.18);"><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Free tier</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Yes (2 daily commits)</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Yes (full features)</td></tr>
              <tr><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;color:#2B211B;">Premium</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">Pro $4.99/mo or $39.99/yr (7-day trial)</td><td style="padding:0.85rem 0.5rem;">$4.99/mo cosmetics + Gems</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:2rem;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 1.5rem;">Where Habitica wins</h2>
        <p style="margin:0 0 1rem;">Habitica's library and customization depth are unmatched in this category: twelve-plus years of community-made content, custom rewards, party battles, and cross-platform sync. If you want one app that holds your to-do list, your habits, and an active community around them, Habitica is the answer.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 2rem;">Habitica also wins on platform breadth: Android and web users have nowhere to go in CardHabit at launch.</p>

        <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:2rem;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 1.5rem;">Who CardHabit is for</h2>
        <p style="margin:0 0 1rem;">CardHabit is built for the Atomic Habits reader who tried 75 Hard and burned out: people who want steady improvement over years, not another 75-day grind, and who would rather do something hard every day than something extreme once. The friend side is built on company rather than surveillance. With CardHabit 2.0, a friend can deal you in on a card from their hand: if you both finish it, you each get a paired foil card with both names on it, and if one of you doesn't, nothing bad happens.</p>
        <p style="margin:0 0 2rem;">If that's not you, Habitica's open-ended customization is probably the better fit.</p>

        <h2 style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;font-size:2rem;color:#2B211B;margin:0 0 1.5rem;">Where CardHabit is different</h2>
        <p style="margin:0 0 1rem;">CardHabit is opinionated where Habitica is open. A fixed deck of cards asks you to think about your day across a handful of areas (in 2.0, five suits: Physical, Mind, Nutrition, Recovery, and Connection) instead of accumulating an unbounded checklist. The randomized morning draw means you don't pick your day from scratch. You're presented a hand and you commit.</p>
        <p style="margin:0;">The social mechanic is different in kind. In Habitica, friends are your party and you fight bosses together. In CardHabit, friends share the same small piece of a real day: you deal a friend in on a card from your hand, by share link if they don't have the app, and you each finish it on your own. Finish it together and you each keep a paired foil card in your binder. Deal a friend in arrives with CardHabit 2.0.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Ornament />

    <RelatedPages current="/vs/habitica" />

    <Ornament />

    <GetTheApp />
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
